s://github.com/dcommander","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"dcommander","id":651941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTk0MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/651941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander","html_url":"https://github.com/dcommander","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"907bec53d751ca9bf524b4cc91210c21d3582f2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/commits/907bec53d751ca9bf524b4cc91210c21d3582f2e","html_url":"https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/commit/907bec53d751ca9bf524b4cc91210c21d3582f2e"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"0ff47f0b46924ea1aaf04092ba1d0c0f83f93b10","node_id":"C_kwDOAl6yRtoAKDBmZjQ3ZjBiNDY5MjRlYTFhYWYwNDA5MmJhMWQwYzBmODNmOTNiMTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"DRC","email":"information@libjpeg-turbo.org","date":"2026-04-11T13:21:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"DRC","email":"information@libjpeg-turbo.org","date":"2026-04-11T15:39:12Z"},"message":"jpeg_crop_scanline: Throw error if raw data output\n\njpeg_crop_scanline() doesn't actually work with raw data output.  If\nbuffered-image mode is disabled and raw data output is enabled, the\nfunction throws JERR_BAD_STATE because the global state is DSTATE_RAW_OK\nrather than DSTATE_SCANNING.  However, due to an oversight in\n8162eddf041e0be26f5c671bb6528723c55fed9d (libjpeg-turbo 2.1.4), enabling\nboth buffered-image mode and raw data output allowed the caller to sneak\nthrough the gates.  Thus, executing the following sequence with the same\nlibjpeg API instance caused a use-after-free issue:\n\n- jpeg_start_decompress(&cinfo)\n  * calls j*init_upsampler() to allocate the upsampler (cinfo.upsample)\n- jpeg_abort_decompress(&cinfo)\n  * frees the upsampler\n- cinfo.raw_data_out = TRUE\n- cinfo.buffered_image = TRUE\n- jpeg_start_decompress(&cinfo)\n  * does not call j*init_upsampler(), because cinfo.raw_data_out == TRUE\n- jpeg_crop_scanline(&cinfo, &xoffset, &width)\n  where xoffset and width would cause any of the component planes to be\n  cropped to a width of 1 sample\n  * fails to catch that raw data output is enabled, because the global\n    state is DSTATE_BUFIMAGE rather than DSTATE_RAW_OK\n  * fails to catch that the previous decompression operation was\n    aborted, because cinfo->output_scanline is 0 (since\n    jpeg*_read_scanlines() was never called)\n  * calls j*init_upsampler() with\n    cinfo->master->jinit_upsampler_no_alloc == TRUE, which tells\n    j*init_upsampler() to reuse the upsampler\n  * j*init_upsampler() tries to reuse the upsampler that has already\n    been freed.\n\nAny application that did this could never work properly.  (The best it\ncould hope for is a bogus output image or an error.)  Thus, this\nrepresented an opportunity for API hardening rather than a security\nvulnerability.\n\nThis commit also modifies the jpeg_crop_scanline() documentation to\nclarify that the function doesn't work with raw data output.\n(Previously, the documentation was subtle on that point.  It says that\njpeg_crop_scanline() must be called between jpeg_start_decompress() and\njpeg*_read_scanlines(), which implies that it can't be called between\njpeg_start_decompress() and jpeg*_read_raw_data().)","tree":{"sha":"7c4e6358dbff4f934e1cd40ac97a18152488f9d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/git/trees/7c4e6358dbff4f934e1cd40ac97a18152488f9d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/git/commits/0ff47f0b46924ea1aaf04092ba1d0c0f83f93b10","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/commits/0ff47f0b46924ea1aaf04092ba1d0c0f83f93b10","html_url":"https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/commit/0ff47f0b46924ea1aaf04092ba1d0c0f83f93b10","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/commits/0ff47f0b46924ea1aaf04092ba1d0c0f83f93b10/comments","author":{"login":"dcommander","id":651941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MTk0MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/651941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander","html_url":"https://github.com/dcommander","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcommander/subscriptions